### Syllabus Structure

<p>The syllabus is organized into five core topics consisting of both standard core content and advanced high-level extension topics (SL Core & HL Extensions):</p>

::: {.callout-note}
## Syllabus Breakdown
::: {.callout-note collapse="true"}
## Topic 1: Number and algebra
**1.1**: Operations in standard form<br/>
**1.2**: Arithmetic sequences and series<br/>
**1.3**: Geometric sequences and series<br/>
**1.4**: Financial applications<br/>
**1.5**: Laws of exponents and logarithms<br/>
**1.6**: Simple deductive proofs<br/>
**1.7**: Rational exponents<br/>
**1.8**: Infinite geometric series<br/>
**1.9**: Binomial theorem<br/>
**1.10**: Permutations and combinations [AHL]<br/>
**1.11**: Partial fractions [AHL]<br/>
**1.12**: Complex numbers in Cartesian form [AHL]<br/>
**1.13**: Polar and Euler forms of complex numbers [AHL]<br/>
**1.14**: Conjugate roots of polynomials [AHL]<br/>
**1.15**: Proof by mathematical induction [AHL]<br/>
**1.16**: Systems of linear equations [AHL]

:::

::: {.callout-note collapse="true"}
## Topic 2: Functions
**2.1**: Straight lines: equations, gradient, intercepts<br/>
**2.2**: Concept of a function: domain, range, notation<br/>
**2.3**: Graphs of functions<br/>
**2.4**: Key features of graphs<br/>
**2.5**: Composite and inverse functions<br/>
**2.6**: Quadratic functions and their graphs<br/>
**2.7**: Quadratic equations and discriminant<br/>
**2.8**: Reciprocal functions and graphs<br/>
**2.9**: Exponential and logarithmic functions<br/>
**2.10**: Solving equations graphically and analytically<br/>
**2.11**: Transformations of graphs<br/>
**2.12**: Factor and remainder theorems [AHL]<br/>
**2.13**: Rational functions [AHL]<br/>
**2.14**: Odd and even functions [AHL]<br/>
**2.15**: Solving inequalities [AHL]<br/>
**2.16**: Advanced graph transformations and modulus functions [AHL]

:::

::: {.callout-note collapse="true"}
## Topic 3: Geometry and trigonometry
**3.1**: Distance and midpoint in 3D space<br/>
**3.2**: Right-angled trigonometry<br/>
**3.3**: Sine and cosine rules, area of a triangle<br/>
**3.4**: Radian measure, arc length, sector area<br/>
**3.5**: Unit circle trig definitions<br/>
**3.6**: Pythagorean identity and double angle formulae<br/>
**3.7**: Trigonometric graphs<br/>
**3.8**: Solving trigonometric equations<br/>
**3.9**: Reciprocal trigonometric functions [AHL]<br/>
**3.10**: Compound and double angle identities [AHL]<br/>
**3.11**: Vectors: position, displacement, magnitude [AHL]<br/>
**3.12**: Scalar product of vectors [AHL]<br/>
**3.13**: Vector product of vectors [AHL]<br/>
**3.14**: Vector equations of lines in 2D and 3D [AHL]<br/>
**3.15**: Line intersections in 3D [AHL]<br/>
**3.16**: Kinematics applications of vectors [AHL]<br/>
**3.17**: Vector equations of planes [AHL]<br/>
**3.18**: Intersections of lines and planes, intersections of planes [AHL]

:::

::: {.callout-note collapse="true"}
## Topic 4: Statistics and probability
**4.1**: Population, sampling, discrete and continuous data<br/>
**4.2**: Data presentation: frequency tables, histograms, box plots<br/>
**4.3**: Measures of central tendency and dispersion<br/>
**4.4**: Linear correlation of bivariate data<br/>
**4.5**: Probability of events, Venn and tree diagrams<br/>
**4.6**: Independent and mutually exclusive events<br/>
**4.7**: Discrete random variables and expectation<br/>
**4.8**: Binomial distribution<br/>
**4.9**: Normal distribution<br/>
**4.10**: Regression line and predictions<br/>
**4.11**: Conditional probability<br/>
**4.12**: Standardized normal variables (z-scores)<br/>
**4.13**: Bayes' theorem [AHL]<br/>
**4.14**: Probability density functions for continuous random variables [AHL]

:::

::: {.callout-note collapse="true"}
## Topic 5: Calculus
**5.1**: Concept of limits<br/>
**5.2**: Increasing and decreasing functions<br/>
**5.3**: Derivative of power functions and basic rules<br/>
**5.4**: Tangents and normals equations<br/>
**5.5**: Indefinite integration as anti-differentiation<br/>
**5.6**: Derivative rules: product, quotient, and chain rules<br/>
**5.7**: Second derivative, concavity, points of inflection<br/>
**5.8**: Local maximum and minimum points<br/>
**5.9**: Kinematic applications<br/>
**5.10**: Indefinite integrals of standard functions<br/>
**5.11**: Definite integrals and area under a curve<br/>
**5.12**: Continuity and differentiability at a point [AHL]<br/>
**5.13**: Limits of indeterminate forms and L'Hopital's rule [AHL]<br/>
**5.14**: Implicit differentiation and related rates [AHL]<br/>
**5.15**: Derivatives of reciprocal and inverse trig functions [AHL]<br/>
**5.16**: Integration by substitution and parts [AHL]<br/>
**5.17**: Volumes of revolution [AHL]<br/>
**5.18**: First-order differential equations [AHL]<br/>
**5.19**: Maclaurin series expansions [AHL]

:::
